<section class="case-section">
  <div class="case-section__head"><span class="mono" data-reveal>Context</span><h2 class="display-s" data-split>She isn’t derelict. She’s staffed.</h2></div>
  <div class="case-section__body prose" data-reveal>
    <p>SHIPLESS is a sci-fi survival dice crawler for one to four players. A shared deck of chapters tells the story of the Erebus — a mining hauler whose crew didn’t die, they <em>changed</em>. Every turn the ship deals you a new chapter: a locked door, a thing in the dark, a crewmate who is almost still a person. You answer with dice — yours and the crew’s — and live with what they roll. Death is permanent. The ship does not care whether you make it.</p>
    <p>It is the distillation of everything I have worked on: Skyweaver’s card economy, Don’t Die’s dice-building, Pocket Knights’ onboarding — built as a small box with deep dread, solo-first, and playable in a lunch break or across a whole night.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-section">
  <div class="case-section__head"><span class="mono" data-reveal>Design</span><h2 class="display-s" data-split>Your die is your character.</h2></div>
  <div class="case-section__body" data-reveal>
    <ul>
      <li><span><b>Six classes, six custom dice.</b> Marine, Engineer, Medic, Scientist, Smuggler, Android — each a die with its own face set. You don’t pick a loadout; you <em>are</em> the roll.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>The CHARGE die.</b> Every round is a spend decision: bank power, force a symbol, unjam a gun, feed an energy volley. Pressure, every turn.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Gear-fear.</b> A Tarkov-style armoury. Carry your best gun in, lose it if you die, bank it if you escape. Bringing it is the gamble.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Shape-coded traits, no twitch.</b> Turn-based and readable at a glance so the dread comes from the decision, not the dexterity.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>One screen is the ship; phones are the crew.</b> Co-op that scales from a solo run to four people passing dice around a table.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

