<section class="case-section">
  <div class="case-section__head"><span class="mono" data-reveal>Process</span><h2 class="display-s" data-split>I had AI agents play it 1,800 times.</h2></div>
  <div class="case-section__body prose" data-reveal>
    <p>Because the engine is pure and seeded, I could point AI agents at it and have them play thousands of full games across every class. The harness found real balance bugs a human sweep would have missed: a co-op difficulty that quietly collapsed <b>11×</b> at four players, and a single content dial worth <b>45 points</b> of win rate. Then it proved the fixes — the same rigour I brought to balancing at Anomaly Games, aimed at my own game.</p>
    <p>The result is a small game that is fair at every player count, and a process I would run again on anything I direct.</p>
